# Git Workflow

Use `main` as the only working branch unless the user explicitly asks for a feature branch or PR.

## Before making changes

- Confirm the repo is on `main`: `git checkout main && git pull origin main`
- Do not create `cursor/*` or other topic branches by default

## After completing work

When the user asks to commit, or when committing is clearly part of the task:

1. Stage only relevant files (exclude unrelated changes)
2. Commit on `main` with a concise message focused on why
3. Push to remote: `git push origin main`

## Do not

- Create feature branches unless explicitly requested
- Open PRs unless explicitly requested
- Push to branches other than `main` unless explicitly requested
